+
+PayPal environment (no credentials are needed for the card checkout; PayPal
+buttons stay hidden until these are set):
+
+- `PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID` / `PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET`: PayPal REST app credentials (secret is server-only).
+- `PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID`: id of the webhook subscribed to `POST /api/paypal/webhooks`.
+- `PAYPAL_API_BASE`: base for every PayPal REST call (default `https://api-m.sandbox.paypal.com`).
+- `PAYPAL_ENV`: `sandbox` or `live`. This alone chooses the browser SDK host
+  (`www.sandbox.paypal.com` vs `www.paypal.com`); `PAYPAL_API_BASE` never does.
+- `PAYPAL_TEST_BUYER_COUNTRY`: in sandbox only, sent to the browser as
+  `testBuyerCountry` and passed to the SDK as `buyer-country=` so test buyers
+  can see Venmo / Pay Later eligibility.
+
+PayPal flow: the browser sends only SKUs to `POST /api/paypal/orders`; the
+server prices the bag, creates a local order and a PayPal order for that exact
+total, and returns the PayPal order id. On approval the browser calls
+`POST /api/paypal/orders/:paypalOrderId/capture`; the server captures, checks
+the captured amount/currency/status against the local order, and only then
+marks it paid and fulfils it — exactly once, however many times the capture or
+a verified `PAYMENT.CAPTURE.COMPLETED` webhook is replayed. Webhooks are
+verified with PayPal (`/v1/notifications/verify-webhook-signature`) before
+they can change any order.
